// This repo's GENERATED files, and the command that rebuilds each from the merged source (epic `epic-eject` T4;
// spell-app's own since epic `repo-split` P8 cut the other repos out of it).
// - Read by `epic worktree merge-main` (`MainMerge.generatorsOf()`), from the checkout being merged:
//   a branch that adds a generated file adds its line here, and its merge already knows it.
// - IN ORDER:  a later one may read an earlier one's output.
// - Each line's keys:
//   - `outputs`:  globs, from the repo's root
//   - `cwd`:  where `run` runs, from the repo's root
// - Snapshots aren't here:  the merge makes one update per package, after these.
// - The same paths are `merge=binary` in `.gitattributes`:  keep the two in step.
// - NOT here:
//   - `yarn.lock`:  the top repo `spell` holds the one install for every repo
//   - `pages.json5` (hand-kept)
//   - the other repos' (Spell UI's and brand's site data, the brand pack, spell's syntax table):  each repo's own list
//   - the bundles the page server builds on demand, which aren't committed:
//     Spell UI's site and the brand pages (`spell dev bundles`)
//   - the epic engine's (the docs bundle, the epics pack, Epic UI's data):  spell-epic's own, built there
// - A new component pack's line is added by `spell dev pack new`.
{
  "generators": [
    {
      "name": "spell libraries",
      "outputs": ["spaces/@spell/library/**/*.lib.ts"],
      "cwd": ".",
      "run": ["node", "cli/bin/spell.mjs", "compile", "@spell/library"]
    },
    {
      "name": "App UI data",
      "outputs": ["app/docs/__data/{components,search}.json5"],
      "cwd": "app",
      "run": ["yarn", "site:data"]
    }
  ]
}
